	"notes": [
		"Kit grid is 4 m and walls are 3.0 m, so the kit-wide scale is 0.75 across and 1.0 up: a wall piece becomes 2 tiles (3.0 m) long and stays 3.0 m tall.",
		"A piece's transform is scale, then yaw (degrees, about +Y), then offset (metres, socket space). At rotation 0 its room side faces +Z and its origin is on the socket.",
		"Kit walls sit on the x = -2 edge of their 4 m tile with the room on +X, hence yaw -90 and offset z 1.5 (the scaled 2 m half-tile).",
		"tiles is a wall piece's length along its run. squash marks the pieces that may be squeezed to 50% to fill a 1-tile run.",
		"opening is a door frame's clear width and top in kit metres, and outer_width its full width: MapBuilder scales a frame across so the opening spans the DOOR run.",
		"per_cell places that many copies in a 2x2 grid inside each footprint cell.",
		"Left out after screenshots: Platform_Metal2, Platform_3Plates and Platform_CenterPlate read as flat grey squares at one tile; WallWindow_Straight's glass imports opaque white; WallAstra_Straight_Flat reads as bare white slabs beside the banded walls; Door_Frame_Square clears only 2.10 m at 0.6 height."
	],
